.TH "SPGEN-INTERNAL_API" "1" "" "spgen 0.1.0" ""
.SH NAME
spgen\-internal_api \- Generates the internal API accessors for a constituent
.SH SYNOPSIS
mix sp.gen.internal_api [options] <READ\-MODEL|AGGREGATE|COMMAND|EVENT|QUERY>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Data access inside one constituent — for its public API, its validators and its tests. Never across a constituent or composite boundary.
.SH Prerequisite
.IP \[bu] 2
The Domain Model (../../../../domain\-model/README.md) contains the read model and, for each lookup accessor, the invariant that makes the field addressable.
.SH "What the generator does"
<domain_object>_by_id/1 through Repo, and one accessor per unique\-field invariant (<domain_object>_by_slug/1, lowercasing the value and delegating to the lookup query). It is reached two ways: as its own generator, and as the dependency of every validator a command generates — together with the read model it reads and the Queries.<…> module its accessor calls, so a generated accessor never points at a module that does not exist.
.PP
What stays out of it by design: technical implementation that belongs elsewhere (a query, a validator) and anything another constituent has to reach — that goes through the public API (./public\-api.md). An accessor the model does not imply (a join, a read across several read models) is added by hand, together with the query it delegates to, and only for a caller that justifies it.
.SH Tests
No test file of its own: the internal API is exercised through the command (./command.md) validators and the public API (./public\-api.md) in the operation test (./operation\-test.md).
.SS "Generated files"
.IP \[bu] 2
services/api/lib/sportipedia/<_subdomain>/<composite>/<domain_object>/internal.ex (by\-id and unique accessors)
.IP \[bu] 2
services/api/lib/sportipedia/<_subdomain>/<composite>/<domain_object>/queries/<_query>.ex (lookup behind unique accessor)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-subdomain\fR \fI<SUBDOMAIN>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-composite\fR \fI<COMPOSITE>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-constituent\fR \fI<CONSTITUENT>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-model\fR \fI<MODEL>\fR
model root, default docs/domain\-model (relative to \-\-root)
.TP
\fB\-\-root\fR \fI<ROOT>\fR
repo root, default inferred from the current directory
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
report the drift, write nothing
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-force\fR
FE: rewrite present generated units in place
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIREAD\-MODEL|AGGREGATE|COMMAND|EVENT|QUERY\fR>
the element: esdm: reference, *.esdm.yaml, kind.name, or bare name
.SH "SEE ALSO"
spgen(1)
